<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <data>
        <!--
          The authorization gate for every checked projection in this addon.

          WHY A GROUP, AND WHY THE METHOD MUST CHECK IT ITSELF. An `ir.model.access` entry does not
          gate an RPC call. Odoo 19 dispatches `/json/2/<model>/<method>` through
          `get_public_method` (odoo/service/model.py:45) and then calls the function; `call_kw`
          takes the same path. Neither performs `check_access`. An ACL bounds what the ORM does
          *inside* a method — it does not decide whether the method runs at all.

          Measured, not assumed. Against Odoo Server 19.0-20260908 with the model's ACL granted to
          `base.group_user`, a user holding only `base.group_user` called
          `agent_projected_picking_company_v1` over `/json/2/` and received HTTP 200 with a
          well-formed projection response. The integration suite reproduces that as a regression
          test, so the gap cannot silently reopen.

          DELIBERATELY UNASSIGNED. This record carries no `user_ids`, no `implied_ids` and no
          `privilege_id`:

            * no `implied_ids` → nothing confers it. `base.group_user` does not, and neither does
              Inventory Administrator or Settings;
            * no `user_ids` → nobody holds it on install, not `base.user_admin` and not
              `base.user_root`, so the projection refuses every identity until an operator
              deliberately assigns it;
            * no `privilege_id` → it does not appear as a selectable role in the user form's
              privilege widgets, so it cannot be granted by accident while configuring something
              else.

          The default state of a fresh install is therefore: the capability exists, and nobody can
          invoke it. That is the fail-closed direction.

          FOR WHOEVER ASSIGNS IT. This is not an "inventory read" permission and must not be given
          to a human role. It marks exactly one non-human identity — the agent's dedicated service
          user, whose reads are bounded by the control plane. Granting it to a person does not let
          them see more than their own record rules already allow, but it does make their calls
          indistinguishable from the agent's in an audit.
        -->
        <record id="group_agent_projection_service" model="res.groups">
            <field name="name">Agent gateway: checked projection service</field>
            <field name="comment">Holds the right to invoke this addon's checked read projections over RPC. Unassigned on install by design; grant it only to the agent's dedicated service identity.</field>
        </record>
    </data>
</odoo>
